    "note": "LATERAL scale from an assumed 3.5 m lane width, applied to the two lane-centre paths fitted from the ground-contact points of 75 real tracks over 1500 frames. LONGITUDINAL scale from an assumed 6.0 m pitch on carriageway A's broken centre line. The four dashes used were verified consecutive and uniformly spaced: their cross-ratio is 1.3477 against the 4/3 expected for equal world spacing, 1.1% off. The pitch itself is NOT measured - a homography absorbs any affine change of world coordinates, so a metric length along the road cannot be derived from one across it. 6.0 m was chosen because it yields an 85th-percentile speed of 52 km/h, the only candidate in a plausible urban range (4.5 m gives 39, 9 m gives 78), and because the measured mark-to-gap ratio of about 1:2 fits a 2 m mark with a 4 m gap. EVERY DISTANCE AND SPEED SCALES LINEARLY WITH THIS NUMBER. Replace it with a satellite measurement between two fixed features before quoting any figure.",
